  "scope": "Stage E, E4a: resolve, availability and the D18 classification read no Profile document. Prior tests migrate per the owner-approved E4a test map (32 retire, 81 adapt-seed, 12 mechanical, 13 adapt-assert), plus the PostgreSQL LIST-fence test approved after the lane run. A test whose subject is gone (a Profile document winning resolve, the Profile-backed port, rows 8 and 10, the document half of row 3, the row-11 shadow proof, the Profile op-5 refresh owner) is removed; a file whose every test retired keeps only its docstring naming the successors, including the helper module pair_shadow_harness.py. Adapt-seed: a test that stored a Profile document to get a credential now seeds the pair as the backfill leaves it, through the shared tests/unit/migrated_pair_seed.py (a Connection whose locator is the Profile blob address, in the status the document state maps to, and a migrated marker naming it); credential names, cache keys, blobs and assertions are unchanged. Mechanical: renames where a test name described the Profile-backed port, the parametrised port list drops profile_backed, and the patched authorize and contract hooks move to the Connection-backed module. Adapt-assert per the map: the D18 evicted and invalidated lists follow the single publication path; fault and race hooks that held the Profile index move to OAuthConnectionStore.list or PairAuthorityStore.read, the reads the successor path makes (the PostgreSQL LIST-fence counter becomes candidate_reads, still 2); a quarantined pair is resolved before it is quarantined because a quarantined pair now refuses; availability reads no index; a rolled-back Connection-less pair resolves to TargetMissing; the rollback rehearsal resolves with the default selector because a document name no longer selects a target. After the independent review, three retired PUT tests in test_pair_admin_mutations.py (test_put_adopts_a_sole_profile_on_its_own_name_and_address, test_put_on_a_same_locator_pair_keeps_the_row_and_the_name, test_put_after_a_delete_reuses_a_single_leftover_document_as_the_mirror) and the requested-name assertion ('work') in test_pair_admin_publication.py return to their origin/main text, and test_an_unreadable_index_refuses_the_whole_inventory is renamed test_an_unreadable_store_refuses_the_whole_inventory (its fault is on the Connection list).",
  "reason": "OME-1209 Stage E4a removes every runtime read of the legacy Profile index after the 2026-10-20 census met the E4 precondition, so tests that drove resolve, availability or D18 through Profile documents can no longer reach their subject that way. Owner decisions 2026-10-20 (spec section 9 Q8-Q11): an absent or none marker resolves through Connections; a migrated pair uses its effective Connection, otherwise the label path; the D18 Profile rows are removed; E4 lands as three PRs. Owner approvals 2026-10-20: the E4a test map as proposed, the default selector in the rollback rehearsal, and the LIST-fence hold on the Connection list. Owner approval 2026-10-20 after review: until E4b the D18 PUT names its compatibility mirror after the pair's one document (D18 section 5.2), so a pair never gains a second document and a pre-E4 rollback stays safe.",
